## 🎯 Security Best Practices

### DO ✅

- Use managed secrets services (AWS Secrets Manager, Vault, etc.)
- Rotate secrets regularly and automatically
- Use IAM roles/managed identities instead of static credentials
- Encrypt secrets at rest and in transit
- Implement least privilege access
- Audit all secrets access
- Use short-lived credentials when possible
- Separate secrets by environment (dev/staging/prod)
- Cache secrets with TTL (don't fetch on every request)
- Monitor for secret exposure in logs/errors

### DON'T ❌

- Store secrets in code or config files
- Commit .env files to version control
- Log secret values
- Share secrets via email/chat
- Use the same secret across environments
- Hardcode secrets in application code
- Store secrets in container images
- Use default/weak secrets
- Grant broad access to secrets
- Forget to rotate secrets

